node_modules/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Local, per-developer configuration. None of the values in it are secrets (the OIDC client id is
# public by design), but the file names one machine's ports and is not the deployment's.
.env.local

# `15-11`: `.env.ux-gate` carries localhost placeholders, not secrets - see its own header.
#
# The `!` is belt-and-braces rather than load-bearing, and the comment that stood here was wrong about
# why: it said this was "the same exception `.env.production` already is", but only `.env.local` is
# ignored above - there is no blanket `.env.*` rule, so neither this file nor `.env.production` was
# ever being excluded. `.env.production` did not even exist at the time (see #32, where its absence
# turned out to be why the published image could not boot). Kept so that a future blanket rule cannot
# silently swallow this file, with the reasoning corrected rather than left to mislead.
!.env.ux-gate

# `15-11`: `ux-gate/` is source; everything it *produces* is a build artifact. CI publishes the
# screenshots with `actions/upload-artifact` rather than committing them.
/ux-gate/screenshots/
/ux-gate/test-results/
/ux-gate/playwright-report/
/ux-gate/blob-report/
